{"files":[{"content":"#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconstexpr uint32_t MOD = 1000000007u;\nconstexpr int TILE = 256;\n\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\nstatic inline uint32x4_t add_mod(uint32x4_t a, uint32x4_t b) {\n    const uint32x4_t modulus = vdupq_n_u32(MOD);\n    const uint32x4_t sum = vaddq_u32(a, b);\n    return vsubq_u32(sum, vandq_u32(vcgeq_u32(sum, modulus), modulus));\n}\n#endif\n\nstatic inline uint32_t scan_span(uint32_t* row, int begin, int end, uint32_t left) {\n    int x = begin;\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n    const uint32x4_t zero = vdupq_n_u32(0);\n    uint32x4_t carry = vdupq_n_u32(left);\n    for (; end - x >= 4; x += 4) {\n        uint32x4_t values = vld1q_u32(row + x);\n        values = add_mod(values, vextq_u32(zero, values, 3));\n        values = add_mod(values, vextq_u32(zero, values, 2));\n        values = add_mod(values, carry);\n        vst1q_u32(row + x, values);\n        carry = vdupq_laneq_u32(values, 3);\n    }\n    left = vgetq_lane_u32(carry, 0);\n#endif\n    for (; x < end; ++x) {\n        left += row[x];\n        if (left >= MOD) left -= MOD;\n        row[x] = left;\n    }\n    return left;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n    vector<vector<int>> blocked(n);\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int i, j;\n        cin >> i >> j;\n        blocked[i].push_back(j);\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        sort(blocked[i].begin(), blocked[i].end());\n        blocked[i].erase(unique(blocked[i].begin(), blocked[i].end()), blocked[i].end());\n    }\n\n    vector<uint32_t> bottom(n, 0), right(n, 0);\n    bottom[0] = 1;\n\n    if (n < 512) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            uint32_t left = 0;\n            size_t obstacle = 0;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                if (obstacle < blocked[i].size() && blocked[i][obstacle] == j) {\n                    left = 0;\n                    ++obstacle;\n                } else {\n                    left += bottom[j];\n                    if (left >= MOD) left -= MOD;\n                }\n                bottom[j] = left;\n            }\n        }\n    } else {\n        const int tiles = (n + TILE - 1) / TILE;\n        // Each diagonal uses disjoint boundary segments. Its implicit barrier\n        // publishes both edges before dependent tiles on the next diagonal.\n        #pragma omp parallel\n        {\n            uint32_t local[TILE];\n            for (int diagonal = 0; diagonal < 2 * tiles - 1; ++diagonal) {\n                const int first = max(0, diagonal - tiles + 1);\n                const int last = min(tiles - 1, diagonal);\n                #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n                for (int tr = first; tr <= last; ++tr) {\n                    const int tc = diagonal - tr;\n                    const int rowBegin = tr * TILE;\n                    const int rowEnd = min(n, rowBegin + TILE);\n                    const int colBegin = tc * TILE;\n                    const int colEnd = min(n, colBegin + TILE);\n                    const int width = colEnd - colBegin;\n                    for (int x = 0; x < width; ++x)\n                        local[x] = bottom[colBegin + x];\n                    for (int row = rowBegin; row < rowEnd; ++row) {\n                        uint32_t left = right[row];\n                        auto obstacle = lower_bound(blocked[row].begin(), blocked[row].end(), colBegin);\n                        int x = 0;\n                        while (x < width) {\n                            const int stop = obstacle == blocked[row].end()\n                                ? width : min(width, *obstacle - colBegin);\n                            left = scan_span(local, x, stop, left);\n                            x = stop;\n                            if (x < width) {\n                                local[x++] = 0;\n                                left = 0;\n                                ++obstacle;\n                            }\n                        }\n                        right[row] = left;\n                    }\n                    for (int x = 0; x < width; ++x)\n                        bottom[colBegin + x] = local[x];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << bottom[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"Combining the incumbent's wavefront tiling with carry-aware NEON scans inside tile-local open intervals should reduce arithmetic dependency costs without adding synchronization.","notes":"Unmeasured integration; controller evaluation required. The serial path handles n=1. Deduplication and zero resets cover duplicate obstacles and blocked endpoints. Lower bounds handle tile-boundary obstacles; scalar tails handle partial widths. Every modular addition is below 2*MOD, avoiding overflow. Same-diagonal tiles access disjoint boundary segments, with barriers between diagonals.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":["8ad10638231442c4","85b460b1a34648e7"],"transformations":["Retain 256-by-256 OpenMP wavefront tiles, compact bottom/right boundaries, sorted deduplicated per-row obstacles, and the small-grid serial fallback.","Replace scalar tile-local open-interval loops with four-lane modular NEON prefix scans, initializing the vector carry from the incoming left boundary and broadcasting the final lane between blocks; retain scalar tails and a portable scalar implementation."]}